<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-hăbĭto</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. a.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to dwell
			in</i>, <i>to inhabit</i> (post-Aug. for habito,
			incolo). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inhabitatur illa regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 17, 20, § 53</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 102, 27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dorienses oceani locos inhabitasse confines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 9, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nobile solum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 116</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnhăbĭ-tantes</span></b> ,
				<i>inhabitants</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				7, 27, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p.
			107</span></i>. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of garments, <i>to
				wear</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 3 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
